# run-issues-poller.env.example — machine configuration for poller.sh and
# pr-watch-poller.sh.
#
# Copy to $HOME/.config/run-issues/poller.env (or point
# RUN_ISSUES_POLLER_ENV_FILE somewhere else) and edit. Nothing here is
# required: with no file at all both pollers keep their built-in defaults.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   launchd hands an agent no environment of its own, and the login files hold
#   nothing run-issues-specific, so under a LaunchAgent this file is the ONLY
#   channel through which a machine can configure its pollers. It is sourced by
#   the poller, which means THE FILE WINS over a variable inherited from the
#   environment — a value set here overrides one exported in a shell.
#
# NO SECRETS HERE
#   Tokens, GitHub App keys and the like belong in $HOME/.config/run-issues/env
#   (chmod 600), which orchestrate.sh and pr-watch.sh source themselves. The
#   pollers deliberately never read that file: they have no use for a secret and
#   they log copiously. Keep this file to paths and host names.

# Which machines may run the pollers. Comma- and/or whitespace-separated shell
# glob patterns, matched against `hostname -s`. `*` allows every host.
#
# Unset, the pollers fall back to a built-in list of the hosts they ran on
# before the gate became configurable, so an existing machine keeps working
# without this file. On any other machine a poller that matches nothing exits 0
# and touches nothing — that is the fail-safe direction, and it is why an
# unedited copy of this file is harmless.
RUN_ISSUES_POLLER_HOSTS="<this-machine-hostname>"

# Where the four log files per poller go
# (<poller>.log, <poller>.runs.log, <poller>.stdout.log, <poller>.stderr.log).
# The plists carry no StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath keys — launchd performs
# no variable expansion in those — so the poller owns every one of its log
# paths, and this one variable moves all of them.
RUN_ISSUES_LOG_DIR="$HOME/Library/Logs"

# Watchlist location. Leave this unset unless the watchlist really lives
# somewhere unusual: unset, the pollers try $HOME/.config/run-issues/watchlist.json
# and then the legacy dotfiles path, in that order.
#
# CAUTION: setting this DISABLES that fallback chain. An explicit override that
# points at a missing file stops the poller with a "watchlist missing" log line
# rather than quietly polling a different repo set than you asked for.
#RUN_ISSUES_WATCHLIST="$HOME/.config/run-issues/watchlist.json"

# Seconds without a state.jsonl event after which a run is treated as stalled:
# its tmux session is killed and the run finalized as blocked. Must stay above
# the longest legitimate single-phase claude call.
#RUN_ISSUES_STALE_AFTER=3600

# Label that marks a finished issue for automatic teardown.
#RUN_ISSUES_CLEAN_LABEL=auto-clean

# pr-watch-poller.sh ONLY: a separate concurrency cap for the PR watcher. A PR
# scan is seconds of work, not the tens of minutes an orchestrator run takes, so
# it can safely run at a higher cap than poller.sh without widening orchestrator
# concurrency. Unset, it falls back to the watchlist key pr_watch_max_concurrent,
# then to global_max_concurrent — so leaving it out keeps the current behaviour.
# Set here, it wins over the watchlist key. See CLAUDE.md section 7.
#PR_WATCH_GLOBAL_MAX=6
